# Stop / pause = pause all AI agents (hard rule)

Operator directives (Phil, 2026-08-09):

> **When I say stop / pause / halt all agents, I always mean AI agents.**
>
> **When I say stop, I also mean pause all AI agents.**

## The rule

> **A bare “stop,” “pause,” or “halt” — and phrases like “stop all
> agents,” “pause all agents,” “halt agents,” or “kill the agents” —
> all mean: pause every Cursor AI agent. Stop spawning Task /
> Multitask children; do not resume stuck AI children; interrupt only
> as the owning parent per
> [`stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc`](stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc). These
> words do NOT mean kill shell PIDs, cargo builds, Playwright,
> `Deploy-*.ps1`, `npm run dev`, Windows services, Hyper-V VMs, or lab
> infrastructure — unless the operator names those processes or
> services in the same message.**

## Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive)

| Operator says | Agent does |
| --- | --- |
| `stop` | Pause all AI agents |
| `pause` / `halt` | Pause all AI agents |
| `stop all agents` / `pause all agents` / `kill the agents` | Pause all AI agents |
| Same + named PIDs / services / deploys | Pause AI agents **and** act on the named machine targets |

Bare `stop` is enough. Do not wait for “all agents.”

## Required agent behavior

1. **Stop AI work** — Do not spawn new `Task` / subagents. Do not resume
   stuck Multitask children. Interrupt only when acting as the owning
   parent per [`stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc`](stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc).
2. **Leave machine work alone** — Do not ask whether to kill deploys,
   Vite, cargo, or services as part of “stop.” Report them only if
   useful for a resume note; do not stop them.
3. **Resume lists** — When capturing work for later restart, list AI
   chats / agent IDs first. Background shells are optional context, not
   “agents that were stopped.”
4. **Explicit exception** — Only kill or stop non-AI processes when the
   same message names them (e.g. “stop and kill the duplicate deploys”).

## Forbidden

- Treating “stop” / “stop all agents” as permission to `Stop-Process`
  on deploy / build / dev-server PIDs.
- Stopping `aic-server-service` / agent services as part of an AI pause.
- Asking clarifying questions about killing background jobs when the
  only instruction was stop / pause (ask only if the operator also
  asked to clean up machine processes).
- Requiring the words “all agents” before pausing AI work.

